office space on the 14th floor than on the 13th floor. But the interesting thing, I found, if I can go on just a little bit more about this, is that in Russia, they take a different approach. In Moscow, rather than eliminating the 13th floor, which they sort of scoff at, they offer a discount for apartments on the 13th floor, that you get a slightly better price. I mean, I don't know what happens when you turn around and need to sell that space again, but, you know, that's the approach they take. How common are superstitious beliefs and behavior in the U.S.? Have you seen any survey data that talks about how many people consider themselves superstitious

