said that they were at least a little superstitious. So I think it's still quite widespread and maybe even increasing, I don't know. Well, and I know I'm not being original here by asking you this question, but are some cultures more superstitious than others? And if so, why do you think that might be? I used to say no to that question, but the more I study the Chinese culture, the more I think that it is very superstitious. They have, I mean, we've already talked about the number superstitions, but they also have superstitions about. the color red, for example, being lucky. And so wedding dresses are frequently red in color.

20
00:12:11.000 --> 00:13:05.000
